  "description": "DML vs rate-equation laser: turn-on delay + relaxation oscillations",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 100,
        "y": -93,
        "title": "DML vs rate-equation laser — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "VP1 fires a 0->2.7 V step (td=1ns) into two lasers",
          "through 25-ohm R1/R2. LD1 is a static DML (L-I above",
          "Ith=0.019 A, slope 0.3); LR1 is a rate-equation laser",
          "solving coupled carrier/photon ODEs.",
          "",
          "Probes p_dml vs p_rate: the DML tracks current instantly,",
          "while LR1 shows a turn-on delay then relaxation-oscillation",
          "ringing as carriers and photons settle.",
          "Set VP1.v2 = 2.0 and re-run: less overdrive ->",
          "longer delay and slower ringing."
        ]
      }
    ],
